  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ef4120e8d7cc4784ba80e7aeb2d6d58d, type: 3}
  m_Name: LoreDump
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Repeatable: 0
  Lines:
  - Text: Harken to the tale of the Father of Lies.
    Speaker: 2
  - Text: "God of mischief and deceit. Born of the j\xF6tnar."
    Speaker: 2
  - Text: Loki! Slayer of Baldur
    Speaker: 2
  - Text: My beloved, why did you let this deed be done? Were you driven by vengeance
      against the All-Father or by the love for your children
    Speaker: 7
  - Text: You suffer yet my bowl is of finite depth. Let me try to save you.
    Speaker: 7
  - Text: "Once more she leaves Loki\u2019s side, carrying the three tokens hung
      from his neck; a scale from the World Serpent, a tuft of fur from the chained
      wolf, and a lock of hair from she who watches over the dead."
    Speaker: 2
  - Text: "These she takes, along with a drop of her beloved\u2019s blood, and mixes
      them with the venom, to birth the Lie."
    Speaker: 2
  - Text: "Slay Odin\u2019s guardian, then free me and free your father."
    Speaker: 7
  - Text: And so our tale begins; when yet another lie is born.
    Speaker: 2
